  [cnst
    'the target of a burnt atom is its subject, GLOSSARY section 0.3, normative: the human operand is the subject of the whole formula, and what is nested inside an item is a standard it works against; so an atom the author wrote works on its own operands, and every item a composite formula produces works on the composite operands'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'subjects compare by burnSame, the equality the burn already has; the fused element keeps the shape it has today'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'H-10 and H-10b encode the reversed behaviour, so they move to one target, by the decision; a test that different targets stay apart is added'
  [/cnst]
